    "answer": "to{} put-back/return/give-back/restore-(to-a-previous-state,-e.g.-defrosting,-reconstituting,-reconciling)/turn-back-(e.g.-clock-hand) | vomit/throw-up | recover-(of-a-market-price)",
    "mnemonic": "Because the hiragana ends with an <ja>う</ja> sound, you know this word is a verb. The kanji itself means <kanji>return</kanji> and the verb vocab version is <vocabulary>to return</vocabulary> or <vocabulary>to return something</vocabulary>. You know you're doing the action of returning someone or something because when you do, they just <reading>sue</reading> (<ja>す</ja>) you because you broke the thing you were supposed to return before returning it.",
    "readingMnemonic": "The reading is the same as what you learned with the kanji."
